WEBVTT

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.820
All right, let's do some fielding practice!

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.030
Focus!

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.990
Okay!

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.700
So much energy, even in this heat.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:19.660
Excuse me.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.710
What if two of us play the same position?

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.390
Take it in turns.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.660
Ukita-san can go first.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.790
Okay!

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.880
Got it.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.080
<i>There are two right fielders now.</i>

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.590
<i>I have to do well here.</i>

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.180
Right field!

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.230
Akane-chan!

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.540
Are you all right?

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.170
I-I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:03.790
There it is!

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.300
Ukita-san?

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.220
Coming!

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:47.020
<b>Looking Ahead to Summer</b>

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.450
I've got a mosquito bite.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:58.490
Same here. I even had bug spray on...

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.300
What do you expect when
we're out there getting dirty?

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.740
Just look at Akane.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:07.260
Scrapes are badges of honor!

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.570
That's a little embarrassing...

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.210
I've got scrapes, too!

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:12.390
Let's ask the teacher when she gets here.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:14.630
See? Here, and here, and here...

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.110
Yeah.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.300
Sensei!

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.090
It got hot awfully early this year.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:21.430
Yeah. It's summer already.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.510
Everyone!

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:30.560
Sorry to spring this on you,
but there's something we'd like to discuss.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.900
So... how about we play in a tournament?

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.230
A t-tournament?

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.470
A girls' baseball tournament?

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:45.730
Yeah! Tomocchi brought it up yesterday.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.460
Well, I'll be going now.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:05.650
Okay. Thanks for your help.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:07.100
You're not leaving yet?

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.310
I want to practice a bit more.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.520
You've improved quite a bit
from when we started.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:17.420
Ah, thank you for saying so.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.250
Now you just have to do it for real.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:22.740
Entering the summer tournament 
would give you valuable experience.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.490
A tournament?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.180
Yes.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:30.830
Of course, you can't go into it
thinking it's just a learning experience.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.300
But I hope we face each other again.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.630
In an official game this time.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:45.490
I vaguely remembered that there 
was a tournament in the summer,

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.750
so I immediately asked
Tsubasa what she thought.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:53.600
I want us to decide as a team whether
we're gonna play in the tournament or not.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:02.730
<i>Strike!</i>

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:05.700
S-So fast...

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.530
<b>National High School Girls' Invitational Baseball Tournament          Round 1: Kogetsu High vs. Nakafuji High</b>

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.750
Kosaka Tsubaki, from Kogetsu High School.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.160
<b>National High School Girls' Invitational Baseball Tournament          Round 1: Kogetsu High vs. Nakafuji High</b>

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.030
<b>National High School Girls' Invitational Baseball Tournament          Round 1: Kogetsu High vs. Nakafuji High</b>

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.450
She was a first-year last year,

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.830
<b>National High School Girls' Invitational Baseball Tournament          Round 1: Kogetsu High vs. Nakafuji High</b>

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:13.660
but that fastball made her the ace 
the moment she joined the team.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:11.790
<b>National High School Girls' Invitational Baseball Tournament          Round 1: Kogetsu High vs. Nakafuji High</b>

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.660
<b>National High School Girls' Invitational Baseball Tournament          Round 1: Kogetsu High vs. Nakafuji High</b>

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.190
That was the first round?

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:19.130
Official games really are on another level.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.920
Do you really think we can handle it?

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.960
It's all about the luck of the draw.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:26.510
<b>National High School Girls' Invitational Baseball Tournament</b>

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:26.760
<b>National High School Girls' Invitational Baseball Tournament</b>

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:27.220
<b>Tournament Brackets</b>

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:27.380
<b>Tournament Brackets</b>

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:27.470
<b>Tournament Brackets</b>

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.430
<b>Tournament Brackets</b>

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.430
Huh?

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:31.470
There are only about 30 schools here.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.780
Yeah, those are all
the schools that participate.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:35.520
You mean...

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.730
We'd go straight to nationals 
without needing to play preliminaries?!

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:44.440
I'd envisioned a high school baseball 
tournament being somewhat bigger.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:50.420
There are far fewer high schools with
girls' baseball teams than with boys' teams.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:53.370
For a long time, there wasn't 
even a girls' tournament.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.160
Really?

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:56.620
Why wasn't there?

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.620
I can answer that one!

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.350
Way back in the Taisho era,

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:07.260
girls' baseball was played for the first time.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:11.610
Playing baseball with a rubber ball
became a trend among girls,

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:15.220
<b>Girls' Baseball Tournament</b>

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:15.220
and the first girls' baseball
tournament in Japan was held.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.420
In the Taisho era?

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:19.520
That's around 300 years ago!

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.690
Wrong.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:24.260
But at the time,
they got a lot of criticism for it,

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:27.020
and baseball was removed
from the curriculum

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.970
because it was considered 
too extreme for girls.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:32.160
That's just how things were back then.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.620
The sport faced a lot
of challenges after that.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:32.780
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:32.830
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:32.870
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:32.910
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:32.950
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:32.990
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.030
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:33.080
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:33.120
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:33.160
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.120
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.120
<b>Women's Professional Baseball</b>

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.160
A women's pro baseball league
was set up after World War II,

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.920
but that didn't last very long, either.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.090
It folded a little over 20 years later.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:44.900
But why?

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:50.090
Women's baseball in itself had
too many obstacles to overcome.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.700
Constant comparisons to the men's game,

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.620
inadequate player development
at the grassroots level...

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:55.550
I guess those were hard times.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:07:00.770
After all that, girls' baseball disappeared 
from the public eye for a while.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:06.690
But that desire to play 
baseball never went away!

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:11.840
Then, in 1995, their hopes
and dreams were realized at last.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:07.480
<b>Friendly Game with
a Foreign Girls' Team</b>

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:07.530
<b>Friendly Game with
a Foreign Girls' Team</b>

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:07.570
<b>Friendly Game with
a Foreign Girls' Team</b>

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:07.610
<b>Friendly Game with
a Foreign Girls' Team</b>

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:07.650
<b>Friendly Game with
a Foreign Girls' Team</b>

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:07.690
<b>Friendly Game with
a Foreign Girls' Team</b>

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:07.690
<b>Friendly Game with
a Foreign Girls' Team</b>

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.400
<b>Friendly Game with
a Foreign Girls' Team</b>

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.400
<b>Friendly Game with
a Foreign Girls' Team</b>

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:16.060
A high school girls' team had a friendly game
with a foreign team for the first time.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.830
And what's more, they played hardball!

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:23.090
That led to the creation of girls'
hardball baseball teams all across Japan.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.940
They started holding tournaments, 
and the pro league was revived.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:30.050
Time finally started
moving for the girls again!

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:34.850
And that's the tale of the fierce battle
that led to girls playing hardball.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:39.310
It looks like this team started 
out as a softball team.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:42.580
There are a lot of schools like that.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:44.900
"Not many of us have
any baseball experience,

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.890
but a number of us do have
experience in a variety of other sports."

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:49.320
Sounds like us... maybe.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:53.780
"Persuaded the school..."

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:56.370
I guess every team's had it rough.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:08:00.970
It looks like lots of schools 
still struggle to find members

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:02.630
because their peers don't get it.

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:05.380
That's why there are so
few schools participating?

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.840
But 30 years ago,
there were no school teams at all.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.300
A team like ours, going to nationals...

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.950
So, are we going to participate or not?

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:20.780
I believe that was the question.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:25.410
It's so exciting! I want to do it!

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.240
M-Me, too!

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.430
It could be a good thing.

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:30.480
I wanna give it a try!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:31.950
Everyone...

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:33.820
Let's give it our all!

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:35.090
I can't wait!

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:36.620
I was pumped up to do this from the start!

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.250
A real game...

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.780
We'll show 'em!

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.000
Hold on a minute. Where are
we getting the money for this?

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.330
Where's it being held again?

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.590
It's in Hyogo.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.650
We'll need to pay for transportation,

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:53.020
and if we win any games,
that'll mean hotel costs.

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:54.010
Yikes...

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.330
What should we do?

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.820
The money situation trips us up again...

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.980
Don't worry, girls!

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:05.990
You won't have any issues with money.

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:08.940
You passed the student council's evaluation!

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:10.710
Right, Tsukumo-san?

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:14.490
Right. Now all you need 
is the school's approval.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.650
Then, that means...

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:19.600
If all goes well, it'll be rubber-stamped
at the next staff meeting.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:23.120
The girls' baseball club will 
be officially established!

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:28.040
So just leave the rest to me!

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:30.880
<b>The Following Week</b>

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:31.870
What?

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:36.800
Like I said, we cannot grant 
permission that easily.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.760
But they've met the requirements!

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.350
Yes, they have.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:42.520
Well, then...

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.520
It just isn't realistic.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:53.440
Baseball Club Trial Balance Sheet

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:49.310
Baseball is a very expensive sport.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:53.440
Starting a club would require 
a great deal of money.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:56.650
This application shows a lack of foresight.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.400
I'll redo it right away!

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.660
There are other problems as well.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:07.330
Are you certain you're prepared 
to lead a baseball club?

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:09.040
I am!

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:14.030
Then how do you intend to divide your 
time between it and the kendo club?

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:19.430
I won't neglect either one.
I'll give both my all!

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:24.140
The school cannot, in good conscience, 
approve such an unreasonable venture.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.970
It's the students who'll suffer
if you overstretch yourself.

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:31.620
I'm telling you that it's unrealistic 
for all of those reasons.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:34.450
But they're all such good students!

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.110
I can't let their determination go to waste.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:39.570
Think about what it is that <i>you</i> ought to do.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.620
We'll put this matter on hold for now.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.310
Tsukumo!

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:56.960
Do you know what Sato High has
to do in order to win at nationals?

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.420
Practice... I guess?

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:00.930
What we need is...

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.640
...a miracle pitch!

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.900
I'll give 'em a taste of the all-conquering
miracle pitch I've just perfected!

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:09.350
Go, Kitty Ball!

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.530
Get serious.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.210
Whoops...

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:22.940
Let's do more pitching practice 
to prepare for the tournament.

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:26.370
Your control will be our main weapon.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:30.830
All right. If we're doing this,
I'll give it all I've got.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:35.010
What could these be?

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.430
Sensei!

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:52.300
How'd it go?

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:53.900
Did we get official status?

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:55.310
Everyone...

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:59.840
I'm sorry! It looks like
we'll need a little more time!

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:02.190
Oh... Really?

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:03.820
Is there a problem?

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:06.190
No, nothing at all!

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:09.540
Don't worry! I'll make sure you're 
all set in time for the tournament!

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:10.390
Okay!

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:12.870
We really appreciate it!

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.090
Bye now!

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:22.050
<b>The Following Day</b>

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.010
<b>Strawberry Milk</b>

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:24.010
She ran into trouble.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.600
You think so, too?

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:29.140
The school's probably being cautious.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:32.550
Sato High doesn't even have
a boys' baseball team, after all.

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:34.210
That's true.

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:37.650
But... does that mean we 
can't play in the tournament?

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:43.920
Well, regardless, our only option is to
trust Sensei and do whatever we can do!

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.490
What can we do?

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:47.570
<b>Strawberry Milk</b>

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:47.570
Practice!

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.200
Practice, huh?

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.770
Practicing is important, but...

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.710
By the way, where's Nakano-san?

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:56.670
<b>Library</b>

00:12:57.310 --> 00:13:00.180
Now's the time for the 
journalist to step up!

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:03.350
Um... Like I said before,
could you keep your voice down?

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.100
Didn't you used to be in the newspaper club?

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.840
Girls' Baseball Association Starting Up from Scratch

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:10.100
I'm in the newspapurr club 
<i>and</i> the baseball association.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:14.180
<b>A Brand New
Association</b>

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:14.180
<b>Fighting Hard With 11 Members!</b>

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:14.180
<b>Playing on a Self-Maintained Field!</b>

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.640
Are you interested in baseball?

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:21.230
Ah, no... It just sounds like...

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:20.480
<b>Overcoming Hardships Together</b>

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:20.900
<b>Overcoming Hardships Together</b>

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:21.570
<b>Overcoming Hardships Together</b>

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.570
Like a fantasy...

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:27.700
Oh! I'm sorry! It's not—

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.310
I think so, too.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:34.440
But this is exactly what 
we've all been doing,

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:38.250
so I want everyone to know,
even if only a little.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:41.710
I want to know more, too.

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.050
Right?

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:47.060
Thank you very much!

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:50.010
Hi, ma'am!

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:51.510
You all looked great out there.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:55.650
Oh, um, ma'am?

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:57.480
Yes, dear?

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.440
Well, there's something 
I've been wondering...

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:11.370
<b>Momoko,
What are you up to?</b>

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:11.370
<b>Momoko, is the teaching going well?
Why not come pay us a visit at home
every now and then?</b>

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:17.330
It's taking a toll on you, 
isn't it, Kakehashi-sensei?

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:19.520
I'm sorry!

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:22.630
The vice principal really 
didn't need to go that far.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:25.340
No, it's my own fault.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:29.300
I thought I was prepared for this, but...

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.530
I guess it wasn't enough.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:37.390
Well, I'm rooting for
the girls' baseball club.

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.550
There's that whole thing with Kurashiki, too.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:41.970
Thank you for that.

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:45.540
But if, realistically, 
it's just too difficult,

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:48.700
there's no reason it has 
to happen <i>this</i> year.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.420
There's always next year.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:55.590
I think part of being a teacher 
is helping them understand that.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.090
A teacher, huh?

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.690
We gotta pull those weeds out, too!

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:25.440
Oh, Sensei!

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:28.260
Thanks for coming!

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.900
What are you all doing? Are those...

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.630
They're sunflowers.

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:34.160
Sunflowers?

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:39.000
Apparently, this field used to be 
next to a big sunflower patch.

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:41.410
Are they in your way?

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:44.750
Oh, no! Not at all!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:48.790
Sunflowers always bloom facing the sun.

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:53.120
We thought if we could help them grow, 
something good might happen.

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.180
It's a prayer of sorts.

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:59.030
It's pretty hard work, though.

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:01.100
If we all pitch in, 
it'll be done in a flash!

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.830
Hey!

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:06.520
We found the perfect thing!

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:11.700
Nice going, Asada-senpai!

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.460
Here it comes!

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.370
S-Senpai...

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.050
You're getting it all over us!

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:21.830
And what's wrong with that?

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:34.430
Now you've done it!

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:36.930
Hold it right there!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.020
I didn't mean to do that!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:43.310
Take that!

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.650
Hold it! Stay right there!

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:51.830
Run!

00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:57.620
I'm so sorry, girls!

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:01.590
I was ready to give up.

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:04.790
I thought this year's 
tournament was out of reach.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:09.650
But I'm over it! Now I've got myself
into this, I'm in it for the long haul!

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:11.060
Let's go to that tournament!

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:13.800
This year's summer is
once in a lifetime, after all!

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:16.440
We'll all work hard, too!

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:19.260
Um, I had an idea...

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.600
<b>The Satogahama Girls' Baseball Association Nine!</b>

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:30.190
Aren't those the girls I see at your 
restaurant all the time, Saki-chan?

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:32.570
Yeah, the baseball team.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.070
They're still just an association?

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.030
What's this? Isn't Kakehashi-sensei...

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:42.580
Yes, she's the advisor for
our kendo club, too.

00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:44.420
What's she like?

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.510
She's a very kind, earnest teacher.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.790
Hey there, everyone!
If this article's piqued your interest,

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.960
I'd like to ask all of you a favor!

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.930
I'm not letting you look at
my homework, Arihara-san.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.410
It's not that!

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:02.670
Since you're so well connected, 
I want to ask a favor!

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:05.530
Wh-What's this about?

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:09.010
This girls' baseball club sounds awesome!

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:10.360
You've got my support!

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:13.570
Sure. I love people who try their hardest.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:16.280
Okay! You just need my name?

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:18.780
Aisaka Koko

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:18.870
Here you go! Here's my autograph.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:18.910
Aisaka Koko

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:22.050
Hmm, does that count as signing the petition?

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:19.030
Aisaka Koko

